I have just mailed conquer patch #4 to comp.sources.games.

It will be a three part shell archive containing two files:

        display.c   : a new display.c file.
        patchV4.04  : patches for the rest of the files.

Simply unshar them to create the two files, then replace the old
display.c with the new and run 'patch' on the patchV4.04 file while
in the source directory.

The major fixes include:
     - enhanced map output from the -p command. [which has been
         relocated to 'conquer' to allow individual nations to
         display the world as they see it.]
     - many bug fixes.
     - a REMAKE compiler option to allow demi-gods the ability to
         start their one world campaign from scratch.
     - makeworld is now done using curses.

Once again you can look at the notes.v4 file for a detailed play
by play of what was done.

